ia.indiatimes.com/photo/133156039.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Rocky Mountain Arsenal National Wildlife Refuge in Colorado has undergone a remarkable transformation from a heavily contaminated chemical weapons and pesticide production site into a thriving wildlife sanctuary. This story explores the Arsenal’s polluted industrial past, decades-long cleanup and ongoing environmental monitoring, while highlighting the return of bison, bald eagles, black-footed ferrets and hundreds of other species.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/colorado-cleaned-up-rocky-mountain-arsenal-after-decades-of-weapons-and-chemical-production-a-15000-acre-refuge-now-supports-more-than-330-animal-species/articleshow/133156039.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/colorado-cleaned-up-rocky-mountain-arsenal-after-decades-of-weapons-and-chemical-production-a-15000-acre-refuge-now-supports-more-than-330-animal-species/articleshow/133156039.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-12T14:03:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133157068,imgsize-94540.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bill Gates is the largest private farmland owner in the United States]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133174598.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/bill-gates-ranks-only-44th-among-americas-largest-landowners-but-he-remains-the-countrys-biggest-private-farmland-owner/articleshow/133174598.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/bill-gates-ranks-only-44th-among-americas-largest-landowners-but-he-remains-the-countrys-biggest-private-farmland-owner/articleshow/133174598.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-12T14:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133174598,imgsize-168853.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Lake Erie fish gather near low-oxygen zones as climate change reshapes habitat]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133175948.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Fish in Lake Erie appear to gather near low-oxygen areas instead of steering clear of them, which reshapes the landscape of their habitat. This unexpected behavior not only changes how fish interact but also contradicts prior theories about their avoidance strategies. With climate change potentially worsening these hypoxic conditions, understanding these dynamics becomes vital for sustainable fisheries management and ecological monitoring.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/lake-erie-fish-gather-near-low-oxygen-zones-as-scientists-study-how-climate-change-could-reshape-their-habitat/articleshow/133175948.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/lake-erie-fish-gather-near-low-oxygen-zones-as-scientists-study-how-climate-change-could-reshape-their-habitat/articleshow/133175948.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-12T13:48:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133176084,imgsize-122498.cms"/></item></channel></rss>